{"repositoryId":451097831,"availability":"available","full":"LBD-Hackers/IFC-LBD","name":"IFC-LBD","description":"IFC.js based IFC to Linked Building Data parsers","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":13,"forks":2,"created":"2022-01-23T12:30:44Z","updated":"2023-06-14T12:40:15Z","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://lbd-hackers.github.io/IFC-LBD/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:24.748Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:24.748Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:24.748Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T20:16:24.748Z","stars":13,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["IFC to Linked Building Data (LBD) is built on IFC.js. It uses the web-ifc model loader and parses out triples in JSON-LD format.","Working with IFC in the express file format, and therefore the IFC.js project is like sent from the sky. It provides tools that make it a whole lot easier to retrieve properties and traverse the relationships of the IFC file, but even so, it is still a cumbersome job to work with IFC.","The minimal Building Topology Ontology (BOT), however, is quite straightforward to understand, and having a BOT dataset in RDF is cool because it allows you to do sophisticated queries it with SPARQL. The resulting JSON-LD-object can furthermore be re-structured using the cool concepts of compaction, expansion and framing. For example, it might be useful to use framing to build a simple tree structure of the graph as demonstrated below:"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LBD-Hackers/IFC-LBD/blob/master/readme.md","fingerprint":"c22ebd67bf84917cdee32eb518ffe849b0d480904cfc88f5d216e7e757d3d0e0","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:24.993Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T20:16:24.993Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"IFC to Linked Building Data (LBD) is built on IFC.js. It uses the web-ifc model loader and parses out triples in JSON-LD format.","so